# public-terms.allow — reviewed lines scripts/check-public-terms.sh admits.
#
# One `path:sha256` entry per admitted line, where the digest is of the whole
# line (its bytes without the line ending). An entry survives the line moving and
# lapses when the line changes, so an edited line is reviewed again. Generate the
# candidates with `bash scripts/check-public-terms.sh --emit-allow` and add only
# the ones a reviewer has read. Say why a line is admitted without quoting the
# term the gate found in it.

